; Protect the count. Winning 42 p. 49 (S-0071-a, S-0071-b) and p. 54
; (S-0078-c); played in Hand 33 (S-0144-b) and, from the bidder's side, in
; Hand 26 (S-0122-c). The trump-set exception: p. 50 (S-0073-c).
; Rule, in our words: a setter following a lead of the bidder's that no live
; tile outside his hand can beat in its suit (a double, the top trump), with a
; choice of followers, follows with one that is not count and keeps the count
; tile guarded for the bidder's off. The exception is the trump set: when his
; partner holds the trumps and is still to play, the trick may be his, and the
; count goes on it (pounce, trump-set.silas).
; Replaces gates/c08-no-count-on-the-double.silas and
; gates/c13b-protect-the-count.silas. How it differs: the gates take non-trump
; doubles only, and C13b exactly two followers; the book protects on the top
; trump too (Hand 33 trick 1: the 4-2 played, the 4-1 kept), and with any
; number of followers. Neither gate has the trump-set exception, under which
; the book's reading of a count follow as a void fails (S-0078-c). The reading
; itself is another seat's play (GAPS.md, policy likelihood). Against a bid
; of marks count does not matter; the defender keeps his pair instead
; (low-from-a-pair.silas).

(include book)

(policy protect-the-count
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule follow-the-master-without-count
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair me) (chair pard) (domino led) (context q) (domino plain) (domino counted))
        (out plain)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (setter me)
          (not (every-trick))
          (partner me pard)
          (bidder-led led)
          (led-context q)
          (not (loses-in led q))
          (none (roles (domino over)) (own-legal over) (beats over led q))
          (none (roles) (trump-set pard) (none (roles (domino his)) (trick-play pard his)))
          (follower plain)
          (count plain 0)
          (follower counted)
          (count-tile counted))))))
